{
 "answer": "The maximal hybrid is maximal over MECHANISMS, not over control planes. Seven singular planes partition authority: CP-IDENTITY (A2 typed registry SSOT + A1 whole-object overlay that cannot introduce ids; A1 silent-unlisted skip rejected), CP-PIN (A3 lockfile + lifecycle SM + cache invalidation; A3 index-as-identity rejected), CP-ACTIVATE (A4 index-derived + activate/deactivate + budget REFUSE; gateway-as-discovery-SSOT and permission-at-select rejected), CP-DISPATCH (A5 ledger, at-least-once+idempotent, one reducer, one-winner claim), CP-VENDOR (A6 three tiers, FAIL-LOUD on missing GUARANTEED), CP-PERMIT (A7 single choke point every invocation crosses), CP-SURFACE (A8 jobs-to-be-done + what/meaning/next-action error contract). The capability-to-authority table is the proof: each capability class has exactly one authority. The first construct that is not expressible is composing A2 identity SSOT with A3 index-as-identity SSOT; we stop there rather than union them. A1-A8 DESIGN.json are present on this tree; each borrowed mechanism cites the live dossier (A8 under report.question) plus the catalog design-unit title/tests_required. A planted cite of an absent A3 MISSING-DOSSIER.json must fail.",
